      theta0 = [0, pi/2, 0, pi, pi, 0].
    These fixed zero-position compensations are embedded in the URDF origins,
    so callers pass the normal joint angles q_i without adding them again.
    Each URDF origin is the exact fixed transform A_i(0), followed by a
    revolute joint about the local +Z axis.  The nontrivial rpy values are
    exact URDF fixed-axis RPY decompositions of Rx(alpha_i) Rz(theta0_i).

    Hard limits and maximum velocities are from the EFORT ER400-3700
    product sheet (2026/03), converted from degrees and degrees/second to
    radians and radians/second.  The source effort values are retained;
